  "$layerOrderComment": "Canonical draw order, back to front. Depth comes from layering rather than from bigger images. A map need not use every layer, but any layer it does use must be named from this list \u2014 an unlisted name is a typo or a taxonomy drift.",
  "$objectLayerComment": "Object layer holding placed world objects. Each object's `type` must name an ObjectDef in src/data/objects \u2014 the content validator enforces it.",
  "$pulseLayerComment": "Optional per-map `pulseLayer`: an object layer of City Pulse slots. Every slot is a named, uniquely named object with a `type` (wall, corner, shopfront, crowd). Districts list the slots they offer under pulse_slots and the validator checks they exist.",
  "$doorComment": "Any spawn-layer object named door_* or typed `door` is a door and must be 32x48 (player height = door height, design system \u00a72). The map validator warns otherwise.",
  "$shapeLayerComment": "Optional per-map `shapeLayer` (generated maps): objects typed `solid` (pixel-precise blocks the feet cannot cross) and `occluder` (a cut-out drawn above whoever stands behind it; properties image + baseY). Written by scripts/import-map.mjs."
